Box86 patch 25 -- correct the remaining Wine 11 Wayland listener ABI mismatch.

Apply after patch 24 to Box86 commit 0579f8b9 plus the FINALPLAY15 complete
patch and patches 17--24.

AUDIT EVIDENCE

The generated Wine 11 text-input-unstable-v3 protocol header declares
zwp_text_input_v3_listener.delete_surrounding_text as exactly:

    (data, object, uint32_t before_length, uint32_t after_length)

Patch 17 instead declared an additional pointer between object and the two
lengths and used RunFunctionFmt "pppuu". The i386 cdecl guest could ignore the
extra tail word, but the function installed into native armhf libwayland still
had the wrong C callback type and shifted after_length into the wrong guest
argument.

A complete callback-count/type comparison against the exact Wine build headers
found five other table-length differences. Wine binds wl_compositor at version
4, wl_seat at version 5 and zwlr_data_control_manager_v1 at version 1, so the
newer wl_surface, wl_touch and data-control primary-selection events are not
legal on the live objects and are deliberately not claimed here.

FIX

Use the exact four-argument callback and "ppuu" guest format. Publish this
listener table through the same release/acquire scheme as the callback classes
corrected in patches 23+24. This listener is registered from Wine's text-input
setup and dispatched on its Wayland event thread, so the ordinary pointer store
had the same cross-thread publication weakness.

